A||||3||sparks||Feiro Takes on Ford F150 Head on||||8||
Z||000000||sparks||02-02-2001||11:27 AM||||Had an accident in my Fiero head on with a Ford truck.  Luckily no one was hurt but the vehicles themselves.<P>I was headed to work and the wind had been blowing the snow around pretty good the night before.  So snow was drifted across the state road pretty good, several inches deep, Fiero was dragging, and they only way thru for me was to follow the ruts from vehicles before me.<P>Just before I reached the intersection that was cleared I was stuck in a rut of snow 8-12" deep and my neighbor was coming at me stuck in the same rut.  His left front side and my left front side were in the same rut, neither of us could steer out of it.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">  As a side note, my wife in front of me in my Jeep was able to get out of the oncoming truck's way.  Basically we slid into each other on the ice since we were only going straight and couldn't stop.<P>Police officer didn't place any blame other than the weather and the snow plow driver that had been playing at the intersection on another state highway decided to plow the road after we colided.  If he'd only plowed it like it should've been then we wouldn't have colided.<P>Anyway I talked to the truck's owner last nite, he said that he not only needs a front bumper but his steering and suspension are messed up!  All I need is a left front fender, nose, and hood.  The car seemed to drive fine.  He was pretty amazed that he suffered more damage than I did in my "little car".  Score one for the Fiero, plastic cars rule!  <P>I'm going to have it checked to make sure that there's nothing wrong with the space frame and whatnot since I'm having some work done on it by a Fiero mechanic anyway.<P>Coulda been worse!<P>------------------<BR><BR>Adam Sparks||||reg||8
Z||000001||2xsess||02-02-2001||12:27 PM||||Yep could have been worse, glad to hear that no one was hurt.<P>Ummm...you misspelled Fiero in the topic.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>AOL IM : Only2xsess<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/2xsess.gif">    <BR> <A HREF="http://kresgeus.homestead.com/FieroPage.html" TARGET=_blank>http://kresgeus.homestead.com/FieroPage.html</A>||||reg||1
Z||000002||lou_dias||02-02-2001||12:36 PM||||A 96 GMC Suburban hit my 87 GT @30mph on the left front quarter and into the driver's side door.  My car held it's ground and the GMC bounced off and into a telephone pole and got totalled.  My car got fixed.  It was my little brother driving so I don't know the exact point of impact but I needed a new door and lower A-arm and fender and a slight pulling of the frame near the A-pillar I think.  my door didn't cave in at all on the inside, but the outside was destroyed.||||reg||1
